pra: 0203 - display power honesty: real power transitions, notifications, read-back

Provenance: T23/ring66 falsified 0202's host-state lever (claim-0202 K5): the
advertised MultitouchHostStateKeys produced ZERO host-state pushes — backboardd
read the service (40 property pushes again) but never drove ScreenOn etc., and
touch still only worked after a synthetic power press. The T21-era tracev3
already showed the actual gate: SpringBoard's asserted BKSHIDUISensorMode
(score 4108) carries `digitizerEnabled: NO; displayState: off` from the BLS
`idle timer` sleep, and only a wake event flips it to YES/on. The kernel has
been LYING about display power since 0179's `a5fb_keep_on=1` (ring65/66:
`powerreq n=N arg=0 off=1 keep=1 applied=1` every boot — the off request is
REFUSED, the panel stays lit while userland believes `displayState: off`).
That state split is what latches the digitizer off. 0203 makes the framebuffer
tell the truth so the idle-timer sleep mode never latches at boot.

BASE: work/0202/SweetFramebuffer-pre0202.cpp (= the post-0202 CI build tree
file — 0202 touches no framebuffer file, cmp rc=0, evidence-0202 section 2).
This is the first patch to touch SweetFramebuffer.cpp since 0171/0201; the
context anchors are the 0201 additions (fPowerReq/fUserlandOff) so a drift in
the base would refuse loudly (fuzz=0).

WHAT CHANGES (three items, digitizer-gate-2026-11-22.md section 4 0203):
 1. NOTIFICATION CONTRACT (honest by default): new AppleCLCD::notifyAll()
    walks every open IOMobileFramebufferUserClient and calls notify(type,
    values, count) — notify() already returns silently when the client has no
    function registered for the type (fFunc[type]==0) or no port, so a type
    with no subscriber costs one null check. On every APPLIED power transition
    (off != previous fPowerOff, i.e. the keep_on path did NOT swallow it) the
    kernel now: publishes the read-back property `DisplayPowerOff` = true/false
    (setProperty, kOSBoolean) so the divergence is queryable; logs
    `SWEET FB: power change notified (off=N)` once per transition; and calls
    notifyAll(0..7, {off,0}, 2) for EVERY registered type (8 types, bounded
    by SWEET_FB_NOTIFY_TYPES). No client registers today (ring65/66 notifyreg
    = 0 lines), so this is a zero-cost contract: the first real subscriber's
    type shows up in 0201's notifyreg log and its payload can be shaped then.
    The vsync fan-out (type 5, 6 words) is unchanged.
 2. READ-BACK: `DisplayPowerOff` property above (item 1), kept in sync on
    every applied transition.
 3. COMMAND-LINE (NOT this patch — the flash step): drop `a5fb_keep_on=1`
    from the cmdline so RequestPowerChange(0) actually applies. With keep_on
    gone the panel really goes dark when backboardd asks for sleep, and the
    wake path must work — that is exactly what 0203 tests. The A5XELTE
    display-off-ignored line becomes unreachable only when keep_on is absent.
    RULE: keep the 11 critical args; the flash gate passes (they are still
    all present).

MARKER (workflow assert): `SWEET FB: power change notified` — contiguous
literal, one per applied transition backed by the 0201 `powerreq` lines.

